<!--
  rev_grant main form. Shape copied from Entities/rev_errorlog/FormXml/main/, which is live in
  REV-GrantApplications-DEV; every control classid was harvested from a form in that environment
  and matched to the attribute type it is used with, so none is inferred (IMP-0014 shipped three
  dropdowns with no options from one guessed classid).

  EVERY LABEL IS THE ATTRIBUTE'S OWN AUTHORED displayname, VERBATIM. No test asserts label text
  (IMP-0015), so this is a V4 review item: eleven fields once shipped labelled "Wellbeing
  Answer 1" while the real survey question sat in the attribute's own description.

  SECTION ORDER FOLLOWS THE RECORD'S LIFECYCLE - award, acceptance, payment and impact - so a
  screen-reader user meets the fields in the order the process uses them (TAD section 8).

  rev_signedpdfurl uses the PLAIN single-line-text control, not the formatted one used by
  rev_email/rev_phone. The formatted control was a GUESS about which control renders a
  Format=url column as a link, and a guessed control classid is exactly what shipped three
  dropdowns with no options (IMP-0014). The plain control is proven on 32 committed columns.
  The column keeps Format=url - a schema enum the import validates loudly rather than
  silently - so link rendering is left to the platform's own default for that format.

  rev_name and rev_docusignenvelopeid are disabled: one is platform-generated, the other is
  written only by the acceptance flow that WBS 3.2 will build.
-->
